{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#prop:dc-ch7-2-5","title":"prop:dc-ch7-2-5","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.md","line":95,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.tex#prop:dc-ch7-2-5","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#def:dc-ch7-2-4]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-4-finite]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-5-pos]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.tex","label":"prop:dc-ch7-2-5","line":138,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[$d$ is a metric]\n\n  \\label{prop:dc-ch7-2-5}\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch7-2-4}\n\n  \\dcref{ch7:2.5}\nWith the distance $d$, $M$ is a metric space, that is:\n  1. $d(p,r)\\le d(p,q)+d(q,r)$,\n  2. $d(p,q)=d(q,p)$,\n  3. $d(p,q)\\ge 0$, and $d(p,q)=0\\iff p=q$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch7-2-4-finite, lem:dc-ch7-2-5-pos}\n\\sketch Reversal and concatenation of curves give symmetry and the triangle inequality, while constant curves give $d(p,p)=0$ and finiteness follows from \\cref{lem:dc-ch7-2-4-finite}. The separation axiom is \\cref{lem:dc-ch7-2-5-pos}.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[<span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d$\">$d$</span> is a metric] <p></p><span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a64632d6368372d322d35\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23def%3Adc-ch7-2-4\">↗ def:dc-ch7-2-4</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch7:2.5</span></span>With the distance <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d$\">$d$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> is a metric space, that is: 1. <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d(p,r)\\le d(p,q)+d(q,r)$\">$d(p,r)\\le d(p,q)+d(q,r)$</span>, 2. <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d(p,q)=d(q,p)$\">$d(p,q)=d(q,p)$</span>, 3. <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d(p,q)\\ge 0$\">$d(p,q)\\ge 0$</span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d(p,q)=0\\iff p=q$\">$d(p,q)=0\\iff p=q$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-2-4-finite\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-2-4-finite</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-2-5-pos\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-2-5-pos</a> \\sketch Reversal and concatenation of curves give symmetry and the triangle inequality, while constant curves give <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d(p,p)=0$\">$d(p,p)=0$</span> and finiteness follows from <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-2-4-finite\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-4-finite\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368372d322d342d66696e697465\">section 1</a>. The separation axiom is <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-2-5-pos\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-5-pos\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368372d322d352d706f73\">section 1</a>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-5-pos","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#prop:dc-ch7-2-6","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#def:dc-ch7-2-4","title":"def:dc-ch7-2-4","label":"def:dc-ch7-2-4"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-4-finite","title":"lem:dc-ch7-2-4-finite","label":"lem:dc-ch7-2-4-finite"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-5-pos","title":"lem:dc-ch7-2-5-pos","label":"lem:dc-ch7-2-5-pos"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#cor:dc-ch7-2-7","title":"cor:dc-ch7-2-7","label":"cor:dc-ch7-2-7"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#thm:dc-ch7-2-8","title":"thm:dc-ch7-2-8","label":"thm:dc-ch7-2-8"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#prop:dc-ch7-2-5","title":"prop:dc-ch7-2-5","tex":"\\begin{proposition}[$d$ is a metric]\n\n  \\label{prop:dc-ch7-2-5}\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch7-2-4}\n\n  \\dcref{ch7:2.5}\nWith the distance $d$, $M$ is a metric space, that is:\n  1. $d(p,r)\\le d(p,q)+d(q,r)$,\n  2. $d(p,q)=d(q,p)$,\n  3. $d(p,q)\\ge 0$, and $d(p,q)=0\\iff p=q$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch7-2-4-finite, lem:dc-ch7-2-5-pos}\n\\sketch Reversal and concatenation of curves give symmetry and the triangle inequality, while constant curves give $d(p,p)=0$ and finiteness follows from \\cref{lem:dc-ch7-2-4-finite}. The separation axiom is \\cref{lem:dc-ch7-2-5-pos}.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#def:dc-ch7-2-4","title":"def:dc-ch7-2-4","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-4-finite","title":"lem:dc-ch7-2-4-finite","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-5-pos","title":"lem:dc-ch7-2-5-pos","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}